  alive today kyoto lets her know that  that was his dad and that he is  following in his footsteps another  important detail that will be very  relevant later on since one of the main  aspects of an goku's character arc is  his relationship with his family and  father he clearly has respect for his  father and says he's honored to have  protected them like his father did in  the past as the girl apologizes for not  believing her grandmother about the  demons then goku is positive again  saying there's no better way to live  than not believing and not running into  demons later we also figure out thanks  to rengoku that this demon was far too  weak to have devoured 40 people and  there is a far more powerful demon on  the mugen train which he'll board soon  and obviously everyone who watched the  movie knows exactly who this demon is he  runs into the vendors yet again and they  want to give him a free bento box he  wants to pay but they insist so he takes  that one for free and buys the rest of  the boxes he promises to tell his father  about them bringing him up yet again  showing he's often thinking about his  father then our main characters make an  appearance as inosuke is shocked by the  iron beast that is the train and  headbutts it to zanetsu's great  embarrassment meanwhile rengoku takes  his seat on the train we see some of the  sickly kids who will play a role in this  arc and the train takes off as if  telling us all aboard the new season of  demonstrator it's officially here then  goku digs in and screams delicious just  like he did in the manga and anime film  however by now in this version we have a  much better understanding of his  character of his kindness positivity and  bluntness it's a completely different  feeling than before and i like it like i  mentioned i feel like we know something  everyone else on the train doesn't about  and goku and it's a cool feeling now  after the new scenes we're watching him  eat as if he were a friend we care abo